{"zh":[{"start":4.11,"end":8.18,"text":"谁能说清未来会是什么样？"},{"start":8.2,"end":12.26,"text":"NASA 科学家把几个气候模型的数据结合起来，"},{"start":12.28,"end":16.33,"text":"这些模型被联合国政府间气候变化专门委员会使用，用来展示气温"},{"start":16.35,"end":20.4,"text":"和降水的模式到 21 世纪末可能怎样变化。"},{"start":20.42,"end":24.44,"text":"这段可视化展示了预计"},{"start":24.46,"end":28.49,"text":"我们可能看到的气温和降水变化，"},{"start":28.51,"end":32.51,"text":"与 20 世纪后期的平均水平相比。"},{"start":36.54,"end":40.65,"text":"升温最多的是北半球。"},{"start":40.67,"end":44.74,"text":"在北美，通常有雪的地方，比如落基山脉"},{"start":44.76,"end":48.82,"text":"和加拿大北部，升温会来得最早、"},{"start":48.84,"end":52.92,"text":"幅度最大。变暖会消除"},{"start":52.94,"end":57.01,"text":"白色积雪的反射和降温作用。"},{"start":57.03,"end":61.1,"text":"反照率降低，正是北极地区升温如此剧烈的原因，"},{"start":61.12,"end":65.14,"text":"因为极地海冰融化，颜色更深的海水吸收"},{"start":65.16,"end":69.16,"text":"太阳的能量。"},{"start":69.18,"end":77.19,"text":"反过来，更暖的海水又加快海冰融化。"},{"start":105.54,"end":109.53,"text":"在全球各地，陆地的升温都"},{"start":109.55,"end":113.56,"text":"比周围的海水更大。"},{"start":113.58,"end":117.57,"text":"水的蒸发有助于让海面保持凉爽，"},{"start":117.59,"end":121.59,"text":"而海洋深处在升温之前能吸收大量能量。"},{"start":133.87,"end":137.87,"text":"在南美洲沿岸外，延伸着一片异常温暖的太平洋海域。"},{"start":137.89,"end":141.93,"text":"一种周期性现象，叫做厄尔尼诺，会带来更多降水"},{"start":141.95,"end":145.95,"text":"在太平洋的那片区域，并影响整个地区的气候。"},{"start":145.97,"end":149.98,"text":"我们在这段可视化里能看到这一点——"},{"start":150.0,"end":154.01,"text":"降水的变化。模型预测更暖的海水"},{"start":154.03,"end":158.03,"text":"和增加的降水会横跨太平洋"},{"start":158.05,"end":162.12,"text":"随着世纪推进，延伸到印度尼西亚。"},{"start":166.23,"end":170.28,"text":"印度次大陆上空的季风会带来更多降水，"},{"start":170.3,"end":174.36,"text":"范围更广；东非"},{"start":174.38,"end":178.41,"text":"和萨赫勒的稀树草原，降水可能增加多达 100%。"},{"start":178.43,"end":182.45,"text":"与此同时，地中海会出现相反的情况，"},{"start":182.47,"end":186.48,"text":"降水减少超过 40%。"},{"start":194.54,"end":198.64,"text":"总体来说，中纬度和副热带的干旱地区预计会"},{"start":198.66,"end":202.72,"text":"降水更少，而中纬度的湿润地区降水可能更多。"},{"start":206.83,"end":210.87,"text":"两极和高纬度地区预计降水也会增加。"},{"start":210.89,"end":214.94,"text":"对北美来说，模型显示北部降水更多，"},{"start":214.96,"end":219.0,"text":"南部更少。"}],"de":[],"en":[{"start":4.11,"end":8.18,"text":"Who can tell what the future will be like?","words":[["Who","谁"],["can","能"],["tell","说"],["what","什么"],["the","这"],["future","未来"],["will","会"],["be","是"],["like?","像"]]},{"start":8.2,"end":12.26,"text":"NASA scientists have combined data from several climate models,","words":[["NASA","NASA"],["scientists","科学家"],["have","已"],["combined","结合"],["data","数据"],["from","来自"],["several","几个"],["climate","气候"],["models,","模型"]]},{"start":12.28,"end":16.33,"text":"used by the UN Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change, to show how patterns of temperature","words":[["used","使用"],["by","被"],["the","这"],["UN","联合国"],["Intergovernmental","政府间"],["Panel","委员会"],["on","关于"],["Climate","气候"],["Change,","变化"],["to","去"],["show","展示"],["how","如何"],["patterns","模式"],["of","的"],["temperature","气温"]]},{"start":16.35,"end":20.4,"text":"and precipitation could change through the end of the 21st century.","words":[["and","和"],["precipitation","降水"],["could","可能"],["change","变化"],["through","经过"],["the","这"],["end","末"],["of","的"],["the","这"],["21st","21世"],["century.","纪"]]},{"start":20.42,"end":24.44,"text":"This visualization shows the expected","words":[["This","这个"],["visualization","可视化"],["shows","展示"],["the","这"],["expected","预计的"]]},{"start":24.46,"end":28.49,"text":"changes in temperature and precipitation we might see,","words":[["changes","变化"],["in","在"],["temperature","气温"],["and","和"],["precipitation","降水"],["we","我们"],["might","可能"],["see,","看到"]]},{"start":28.51,"end":32.51,"text":"compared to the average levels of the late 20th century.","words":[["compared","相比"],["to","于"],["the","这"],["average","平均"],["levels","水平"],["of","的"],["the","这"],["late","后期"],["20th","20世"],["century.","纪"]]},{"start":36.54,"end":40.65,"text":"The largest temperature increases are seen in the northern hemisphere.","words":[["The","这"],["largest","最大的"],["temperature","气温"],["increases","升高"],["are","被"],["seen","看到"],["in","在"],["the","这"],["northern","北"],["hemisphere.","半球"]]},{"start":40.67,"end":44.74,"text":"Across North America, areas that typically have snow, such as the Rocky Mountains","words":[["Across","遍及"],["North","北"],["America,","美洲"],["areas","地区"],["that","那"],["typically","通常"],["have","有"],["snow,","雪"],["such","比如"],["as","如"],["the","这"],["Rocky","落基"],["Mountains","山脉"]]},{"start":44.76,"end":48.82,"text":"and northern Canada, will see the earliest and largest","words":[["and","和"],["northern","北部"],["Canada,","加拿大"],["will","将"],["see","看到"],["the","这"],["earliest","最早"],["and","和"],["largest","最大"]]},{"start":48.84,"end":52.92,"text":"temperature rise. The warming temperatures will eliminate the","words":[["temperature","气温"],["rise.","上升"],["The","这"],["warming","变暖的"],["temperatures","气温"],["will","将"],["eliminate","消除"],["the","这"]]},{"start":52.94,"end":57.01,"text":"reflective and cooling effect of the white snow cover.","words":[["reflective","反射的"],["and","和"],["cooling","降温的"],["effect","作用"],["of","的"],["the","这"],["white","白色"],["snow","雪"],["cover.","覆盖"]]},{"start":57.03,"end":61.1,"text":"This reduction in albedo is the reason why the Arctic region shows such dramatic warming,","words":[["This","这个"],["reduction","降低"],["in","在"],["albedo","反照率"],["is","是"],["the","这"],["reason","原因"],["why","为什么"],["the","这"],["Arctic","北极"],["region","地区"],["shows","显示"],["such","如此"],["dramatic","剧烈的"],["warming,","变暖"]]},{"start":61.12,"end":65.14,"text":"as the polar sea ice melts and the darker ocean water absorbs","words":[["as","随着"],["the","这"],["polar","极地"],["sea","海"],["ice","冰"],["melts","融化"],["and","和"],["the","这"],["darker","更深的"],["ocean","海洋"],["water","水"],["absorbs","吸收"]]},{"start":65.16,"end":69.16,"text":"energy from the sun.","words":[["energy","能量"],["from","来自"],["the","这"],["sun.","太阳"]]},{"start":69.18,"end":77.19,"text":"In turn, the warmer water accelerates the melting of the sea ice.","words":[["In","反过来"],["turn,",""],["the","这"],["warmer","更暖的"],["water","水"],["accelerates","加快"],["the","这"],["melting","融化"],["of","的"],["the","这"],["sea","海"],["ice.","冰"]]},{"start":105.54,"end":109.53,"text":"All around the globe, the land areas show a greater increase in temperature","words":[["All","全"],["around","遍及"],["the","这"],["globe,","全球"],["the","这"],["land","陆地"],["areas","区域"],["show","显示"],["a","一个"],["greater","更大的"],["increase","升高"],["in","在"],["temperature","气温"]]},{"start":109.55,"end":113.56,"text":"than the surrounding ocean waters.","words":[["than","比"],["the","这"],["surrounding","周围的"],["ocean","海洋"],["waters.","水"]]},{"start":113.58,"end":117.57,"text":"Evaporation of the water helps to keep the ocean surface cool,","words":[["Evaporation","蒸发"],["of","的"],["the","这"],["water","水"],["helps","帮助"],["to","去"],["keep","保持"],["the","这"],["ocean","海洋"],["surface","表面"],["cool,","凉"]]},{"start":117.59,"end":121.59,"text":"and the deep depths of the ocean have a large capacity to absorb energy before heating up.","words":[["and","而"],["the","这"],["deep","深"],["depths","深处"],["of","的"],["the","这"],["ocean","海洋"],["have","有"],["a","一个"],["large","大"],["capacity","容量"],["to","去"],["absorb","吸收"],["energy","能量"],["before","在…前"],["heating","升"],["up.","温"]]},{"start":133.87,"end":137.87,"text":"Off the coast of South America stretches an unusually warm patch of the Pacific Ocean.","words":[["Off","离开"],["the","这"],["coast","海岸"],["of","的"],["South","南"],["America","美洲"],["stretches","延伸"],["an","一片"],["unusually","异常"],["warm","温暖的"],["patch","区域"],["of","的"],["the","这"],["Pacific","太平"],["Ocean.","洋"]]},{"start":137.89,"end":141.93,"text":"A cyclical occurrence, known as El Niño, causes more precipitation","words":[["A","一个"],["cyclical","周期性的"],["occurrence,","现象"],["known","被称为"],["as","作为"],["El","厄尔"],["Niño,","尼诺"],["causes","导致"],["more","更多"],["precipitation","降水"]]},{"start":141.95,"end":145.95,"text":"in that area of the Pacific, and affects the climate throughout the region.","words":[["in","在"],["that","那"],["area","区域"],["of","的"],["the","这"],["Pacific,","太平洋"],["and","和"],["affects","影响"],["the","这"],["climate","气候"],["throughout","遍及"],["the","这"],["region.","地区"]]},{"start":145.97,"end":149.98,"text":"And we can see that happen in this visualization","words":[["And","而"],["we","我们"],["can","能"],["see","看到"],["that","那"],["happen","发生"],["in","在"],["this","这个"],["visualization","可视化"]]},{"start":150.0,"end":154.01,"text":"of changes in precipitation. Models project warmer waters","words":[["of","的"],["changes","变化"],["in","在"],["precipitation.","降水"],["Models","模型"],["project","预测"],["warmer","更暖的"],["waters","水"]]},{"start":154.03,"end":158.03,"text":"and increased precipitation to stretch across the Pacific Ocean","words":[["and","和"],["increased","增加的"],["precipitation","降水"],["to","去"],["stretch","延伸"],["across","横跨"],["the","这"],["Pacific","太平"],["Ocean","洋"]]},{"start":158.05,"end":162.12,"text":"to Indonesia as the century progresses.","words":[["to","到"],["Indonesia","印度尼西亚"],["as","随着"],["the","这"],["century","世纪"],["progresses.","推进"]]},{"start":166.23,"end":170.28,"text":"The monsoons over the Indian subcontinent will bring increased precipitation","words":[["The","这"],["monsoons","季风"],["over","在…上空"],["the","这"],["Indian","印度"],["subcontinent","次大陆"],["will","将"],["bring","带来"],["increased","增加的"],["precipitation","降水"]]},{"start":170.3,"end":174.36,"text":"over a wider area, and eastern Africa","words":[["over","在…上空"],["a","一个"],["wider","更广的"],["area,","区域"],["and","和"],["eastern","东部"],["Africa","非洲"]]},{"start":174.38,"end":178.41,"text":"and the savannas of the Sahel, could see precipitation increases up to 100%.","words":[["and","和"],["the","这"],["savannas","稀树草原"],["of","的"],["the","这"],["Sahel,","萨赫勒"],["could","可能"],["see","看到"],["precipitation","降水"],["increases","增加"],["up","达"],["to","到"],["100%.","100%"]]},{"start":178.43,"end":182.45,"text":"At the same time, the Mediterranean will experience the opposite,","words":[["At","在"],["the","这"],["same","同"],["time,","时候"],["the","这"],["Mediterranean","地中海"],["will","将"],["experience","经历"],["the","这"],["opposite,","相反"]]},{"start":182.47,"end":186.48,"text":"a decrease over 40%.","words":[["a","一个"],["decrease","减少"],["over","超过"],["40%.","40%"]]},{"start":194.54,"end":198.64,"text":"In general, the mid-latitude and sub-tropical dry regions are projected to see","words":[["In","在"],["general,","总体上"],["the","这"],["mid-latitude","中纬度"],["and","和"],["sub-tropical","副热带"],["dry","干燥"],["regions","地区"],["are","是"],["projected","预计"],["to","去"],["see","看到"]]},{"start":198.66,"end":202.72,"text":"less precipitation, while the mid-latitude wet regions could see more precipitation.","words":[["less","更少"],["precipitation,","降水"],["while","而"],["the","这"],["mid-latitude","中纬度"],["wet","湿润"],["regions","地区"],["could","可能"],["see","看到"],["more","更多"],["precipitation.","降水"]]},{"start":206.83,"end":210.87,"text":"The poles and high latitudes are expected to also have increased precipitation.","words":[["The","这"],["poles","两极"],["and","和"],["high","高"],["latitudes","纬度"],["are","是"],["expected","预计"],["to","去"],["also","也"],["have","有"],["increased","增加的"],["precipitation.","降水"]]},{"start":210.89,"end":214.94,"text":"For North America, the models indicate more precipitation in the north,","words":[["For","对"],["North","北"],["America,","美洲"],["the","这"],["models","模型"],["indicate","显示"],["more","更多"],["precipitation","降水"],["in","在"],["the","这"],["north,","北部"]]},{"start":214.96,"end":219.0,"text":"and less in the south.","words":[["and","和"],["less","更少"],["in","在"],["the","这"],["south.","南部"]]}]}